{"evt":"knowledge_node_upserted","id":"knowledge:source_chunk:note-mr5d6cvqife#note-evidence:chunk-1","key":"knowledge:source_chunk:note-mr5d6cvqife#note-evidence:chunk-1","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","type":"source_chunk","kind":"source_chunk","label":"game ls20 world model program evidence chunk 1","title":"game ls20 world model program evidence chunk 1","summary":"ls20 ceiling world model (12/13; leaves one auto-changing region unmodeled)\n\npass rate: 12/13\n\nprogram source:\n# World-model program for an ARC-AGI-3 game.\n# Scope of this revision: player_movement.\n#   The player is a rigid linked unit = the (unique) color-12 object plus the\n#   color-9 object physically linked to it. Each action translates the whole\n#   unit by a fixed vector:\n#       ACTION1 -> (dr=-5, dc= 0)   (up)      -- dominant move\n#       ACTION2 -> (dr=+5, dc= 0)   (down)\n#       ACTION3 -> (dr= 0, dc=-5)   (left)\n#       ACTION4 -> (dr= 0, dc=+5)   (right)\n# Every other per-step effect on the board (maze scroll, box clipping, HUD bars)\n# is a separate mechanic not modeled here; those cells are rendered UNKNOWN so\n# they are skipped by the validator instead of being predicted incorrectly.\n\nimport re\n\n_PLAYER_COLORS = (9, 12)\n\n_VECTORS = {\n    1: (-5, 0),\n    2: (5, 0),\n    3: (0, -5),\n    4: (0, 5),\n}\n\n\ndef _action_vector(action):\n    \"\"\"Map an action (string like 'ACTION1' or an int) to a (dr, dc) vector.\"\"\"\n    m = re.search(r\"(\\d+)\", str(action))\n    n = int(m.group(1)) if m else 0\n    return _VECTORS.get(n, (0, 0))","metadata":{"note_key":"note:note-mr5d6cvqife","origin":"overlay/note"},"source_path":null,"section_ref":"note-evidence","chunk_ref":"chunk-1","cluster_ref":null,"created_at":"2026-07-03T20:08:02.747Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T20:08:02.747Z","vec":[-0.04005129262804985,-0.030617889016866684,0.02632487751543522,-0.055637527257204056,0.10433152318000793,0.043779946863651276,0.02507256716489792,-0.022521233186125755,0.0710470